WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.880
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and tonight on
Agents of SHIELD it was ladies night.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.310
Roller Derby on a plane.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.470
Jamie Alexander guest starred as Lady Sif
and Elena Satine debuted as Lorelai from the

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.470
comics.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.590
Naturally there was a ton of comic book and
movie references and the mysterious blue alien

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:28.850
plot thickened big time.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.870
So I’ll explain who Lorelai is real quick,
then we can talk about our top 5 moments and

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.130
then I’ll do a review.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.450
Quick shoutout to my Avengers 2 video that’s
coming later tonight.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:47.630
For my Marvel Tuesday bonus video I’m breaking
down the Age of Ultron teaser footage that’s

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:48.630
coming next week.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:49.630
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.039
Now let’s discuss the weakness of all men.

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.039
Lorelia.

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.179
She’s played by Elena Satine who you may
remember from Smallville.

00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:59.320
She played Mera, wife of Aquaman in an episode.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.069
Funny to see her jump to the other team.

00:01:01.069 --> 00:01:03.260
But this was a way better role.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.780
In the comics Loki used Lorelai to distract
Thor while he was busy trying to build his

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.450
power.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.060
The cool thing is that the story also involved
Malekith the Dark Elf we saw in the Dark World

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.620
movie and the Fire God Surtur.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.450
In the continuity of this episode she had
been imprisoned for the last 600 years after

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.810
being captured by Sif, presumably after those
comic book events I just mentioned.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.640
She escaped during the events of Thor The
Dark World, when Kurse destroyed the Asgardian

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.310
Prison that Loki was also in.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.580
So now let’s talk about our top 5 moments
from the episode.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:40.590
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.229
Number 5 - What Kind of Powers Are We Talking
About?

00:01:43.229 --> 00:01:47.920
So you have to remember that for most of the
SHIELD Agents, Magic or sorcery or even mutant

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.920
based powers don’t exist.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.539
Or at least they don’t know about them.

00:01:51.539 --> 00:01:54.320
So the reveal of Lorelai’s powers does a
couple really cool things.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.479
One, it’s just funny to see all the WTF
is Magic faces, but it also opens the door

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:01.540
for more strange powers on the show.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.939
Which I think is laying groundwork for the
Clairvoyant.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:09.679
That is, just making whatever strange powers
he or she has seem more plausible when the

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:10.679
secret is revealed.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:17.090
I’ll talk more about the new Age of Miracles
that’s coming in my Avengers 2 video.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.680
Number 4 - Sif versus the Biker gang.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.650
This is really the first of many amazing fight
scenes.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.900
It becomes pretty obvious that the ladies
are going to be having all the fun this week

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.290
and I think it’s awesome.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.650
The biker gang fight was as much exciting
as it was funny.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.870
Just watching Sif throw them around like rag
dolls.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.650
And the joke with her pushing the giant RV
with her foot.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.120
That kind of humor is straight from a Thor
movie.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.849
Just the comedy that comes from putting a
super strong asgardian in a fight with regular

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:44.920
humans.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.680
I was really bummed that Sif didn’t get
more action scenes in Thor The Dark World,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.620
and I feel like this episode rectified that
mistake a lot.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.209
She’s such an interesting character and
Jamie Alexander does an amazing job playing

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:56.209
her.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:00.230
I loved that moment when Coulson knew she
was hanging on the outside of the plane just

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.870
because she was so tough.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.360
Number 3 - Coulson questions Sif about Blue
Aliens.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:08.560
There were a lot of comic book references
here, but Sif lets him know that only a one

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.879
species actually visited earth, frost giants
a thousand years ago.

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:15.269
That means one of three things.

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:23.450
Either a frost giant was captured or Nick
Fury acquired one from outer space or Fury

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.629
captured one that originated on earth.

00:03:25.629 --> 00:03:29.510
I don’t know that he would have gone into
space yet, even though Guardians of The Galaxy

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.129
is right around the corner.

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:35.480
So the alternate theory to frost giant or
Kree is An Atlantean.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:39.680
They have blue glowy skin and originated on
earth.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.659
Meaning the theory fits within the logic Sif
presented.

00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:48.250
That dispels my Kree theory, but opens the
door to Skye being part Atlantean.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.260
If you’re not familiar Namor is half Atlantean.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.400
So he has powers and can live underwater but
appears human.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.400
Basically Marvel’s version of Aquaman.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.569
This is big, so let me know if you agree with
the Skye Atlantean theory in the comments.

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:02.150
Number 2 - Sif Versus Lorelai.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:06.110
This wasn’t as big a battle as I expected,
but I award bonus points for the creative

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.160
use of Sif’s sword during their duel.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.799
There were also some awesome comic book references
to Lorelai’s old plot with Loki and how

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:13.970
she used Thor.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:18.160
It’s so much fun to see them bring a comic
book story from the 80s into the modern day

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.840
Marvel Universe.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.390
Remember Asgardians live for about 5000 years,
so 600 to them is like a decade for us.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.010
It would be like us talking about the war
in Iraq.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.910
Something pretty recent.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:33.490
And my number 1 moment - The double double
cross including Coulson and Skye on one side

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:34.850
and May on the other.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:39.050
So many things are connecting Agents of SHIELD
to the plot of Winter Soldier.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.690
First let’s talk about the Coulson side
of this equation.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:45.770
The person he was talking about tracking down,
that person who was “responsible” is Nick

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.770
Fury.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.680
He’s off the grid, but we see him during
Winter Soldier.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.960
So we probably won’t learn what he’s been
doing until the last couple of episodes or

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.170
maybe not until the movie in a couple weeks.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.930
Then let’s flip to the other side with May.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.460
She’s keeping tabs on Coulson for someone.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.680
I’m betting it’s Robert Redford’s character.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:06.990
He’d be one of the few people with security
clearance and power inside SHIELD to know

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:07.990
all about the blue alien.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.330
But now it’s your turn.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.520
Let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:17.660
All the roller derby on a plane fight scenes
or all the comic book references or the blue

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:18.660
alien plot.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.240
Overall I give the episode an A just for amazing
use of a movie character Jamie Alexander and

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.220
a comic book character Lorelei.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:30.250
I hope we get to see her in another Marvel
movie or back on the show next season.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:34.530
Jamie Alexander got way more screentime than
she did in any of the Thor movies and I hope

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:39.720
they expand her role for Thor 3, her character
deserves way more screen time than Natalie

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:40.720
Portman.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.390
And if rumors are to be believed, that won’t
be an issue.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:46.020
I’m saying Portman might not return for
a third movie.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.770
I don’t know what her contract says though.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.949
Elena Satine was also so much more fun that
all of the other guest stars this season.

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:55.330
It’s like the Tom Hiddleston Loki bonus.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:06:00.699
The actors playing villains get to have way
more fun and be way more complex than any

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:01.699
of the heroes.

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:04.330
Not to say that Sif isn’t a ton of fun too.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.699
The only thing I thought could have been done
better was the Men VS Women plot.

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:13.599
I understand that it’s a slam dunk to do
gender humor like this when the villains powers

00:06:13.599 --> 00:06:15.620
are all about manipulating men.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.310
And the jokes were totally funny.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:24.630
But I if you don’t need to make men seem
strong by showing women to be weak, then the

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.720
opposite has to be true.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.900
For example, I don’t think you need a bunch
of weak men in a Wonder Woman movie just to

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.970
make her seem powerful.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:36.160
Just like you don’t need to show a bunch
of weak women to make Superman seem powerful.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.430
That being said, Fitz was so much fun to watch
being drunk in love with Lorelei.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.110
And watching Simmons almost crack Coulson
with the fire extinguisher.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:47.570
It’s too bad SHIELD can’t be this funny
all the time, but sometimes having super strength

00:06:47.570 --> 00:07:11.539
and a bunch of Asgardians makes 
it easier.

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:22.490
So 
in related news, look for that Avengers 2

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:23.500
video later tonight.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.740
You can click here to watch it.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.420
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.840
And you can click here to learn about my previous
Skye Ms Marvel theories.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.190
Now expanded to included Namor.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:36.129
Thanks for watching, see you guys tongiht!

00:07:36.129 --> 00:07:37.090
High Fives!

